{"created": "2026-06-09T15:22:31.381275+00:00", "modified": "2026-06-09T15:22:31.668753+00:00", "id": 20586598, "conceptrecid": "20586597", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.20586598", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.20586597", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20586598", "metadata": {"title": "PID-GraphVAE: 3-D cylinder-wake (Re = 300) CFD dataset for \"From compression to discovery\"", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.20586598", "publication_date": "2026-06-08", "description": "<div>Three-dimensional unsteady laminar simulation of a circular-cylinder wake at&nbsp;Re = 300 (ANSYS Fluent; domain 10D/25D/&plusmn;10D with an 8D span; &Delta;t = 0.01 s, snapshots at every step), accompanying the paper \"From compression to&nbsp;discovery: representations whose structure reveals the governing equations\".</div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div>Contents: cylinder_3d_re300_ds.h5 (time-resolved u, v, w, p fields),&nbsp;cylinder_3d_re300_ds.physcache.npz (precomputed physics-supervision targets),&nbsp;and the 3-D mesh coordinate file. The first 2,000 frames (&asymp;12.6 shedding&nbsp;periods) are used in the paper. Full CFD setup: Supplementary Section S1 and&nbsp;data_prep/README.md in the companion code repository.</div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div>Companion records: 2-D datasets and trained models (10.5281/zenodo.20582405);&nbsp;code at https://github.com/ZerirlKeou/PID-GraphVAE.</div>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Liu, Ao", "affiliation": "Shanghai University", "orcid": "0009-0008-9138-0059"}, {"name": "Wu, Pin", "affiliation": "Shanghai University", "orcid": "0000-0002-1411-1188"}, {"name": "Yao, Yuan", "affiliation": "Shanghai University", "orcid": "0000-0003-3302-4909"}, {"name": "Zhang, Yifan", "affiliation": "Shanghai University"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "20586597"}}]}}, "title": "PID-GraphVAE: 3-D cylind